  "codex_last_message": "Changed [src/server.rs](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/server.rs:1) to add an env-gated `VDB_REQUEST_STATS_PATH` sink that records aggregate request counts plus read/process/write timings without touching the default scored path. Added [measure_official_client_breakdown](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/measure_official_client_breakdown:1) and documented it in [.meta_codex/tools/README.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/README.md:1). I also recorded the cycle in [.meta_codex/research_notes.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/research_notes.md:1) and [.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md](/__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md:1).\n\nValidation stayed official and valid. `run_correctness_test` passed at `1.0000` recall. A fresh official quick benchmark on the kept default branch reached `10669.55 QPS`, so I do not expect promotion from this cycle. The useful new result is diagnostic: the new real forced-cache tiny-base breakdown measured `11791.29 QPS` at `1.0000` recall, with benchmark CPU about `0.58s` versus server CPU about `0.12s`, and server-side cached-search processing only about `0.75 us` per request after the body is available. A matched dummy breakdown only reached `9046.87 QPS`, so the old dummy ceiling is no longer trustworthy.\n\nCurrent score expectation is still roughly the noisy `10.5k-11.8k` quick band, not a `22k+` breakthrough. The next best move is to use the new breakdown tool to replace or redesign the dummy ceiling path first, then test transport ideas that change request delivery / client interaction rather than cache lookup cost.",
